WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.430
It’s pointless.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:10.990
I can see into your soul as if it’s mine.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.700
Now show me your power.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.660
The abominable Number’s power.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:23.810
Damn!

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.090
Go, Number 16: Shock Master!

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.940
Who are you?

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.440
My name in Jin, the Number
Hunter Kaito’s faithful servant.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.780
Kaito?

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.910
I’m taking your soul.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.110
I’m kattobing!

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.410
All right!

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:32.820
I’m not late today!

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:40.430
I powered up my deck with new cards, so I’ll get my revenge on Kaito!

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.600
Why are you gloomy?

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:49.060
I’m not optimistic, Yuma.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.460
You and I are different.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.700
What are you talking about?

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.530
That’s obvious.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:56.600
Yuma!

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:57.220
Good morning!

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.270
This isn’t the time for good morning!

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:00.940
Come over here!

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.280
You’re finally going to tell us today!

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.480
Why all of a sudden?

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.610
What’s this?

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.960
We found it on the Internet.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:16.250
Many duelists have been attacked recently.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.410
And all the victims had Number Cards.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.340
Numbers?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:28.710
To summarize, won’t you
also end up like them, Yuma?

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.070
This has been going on?

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.640
I didn’t know at all.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.840
Don’t lie!

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.340
Tell us the truth!

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.930
Are Numbers dangerous?

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.140
I really don’t know.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.970
Yuma!

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.850
I have to go to the bathroom!

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.480
Hey, Yuma!

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.030
Yuma...

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.070
Yuma, why won’t you tell them the truth?

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.800
Isn’t it obvious?

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.050
I can’t involve them in the battle against Kaito.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.880
Kaito...

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.380
Kaito is hunting Numbers again.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:20.300
Then let’s face him
and take back the Numbers!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.550
You won’t beat him so easily
with your silly ideas.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:29.010
Are you afraid of Kaito?

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.810
You can’t be afraid!

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:36.320
In order to regain your memories, we have to defeat Kaito and collect the Numbers!

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.470
What happens if we lose?

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:42.910
He’ll take your soul,
and I’ll vanish from this world!

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.420
You can’t be scared!

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.580
Good morning.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.910
Good morning, Cat.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.130
You remembered my name.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.760
Who’s Kaito?

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.510
Oh no! I can’t hold it!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.300
I forgot to go to the bathroom!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.910
Kaito? Numbers?

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.690
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.820
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.740
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:25.990
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:33.370
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:39.910
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:46.470
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.350
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.480
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.360
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.650
Everyone is not the same

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:03.570
That’s the reason for living

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:08.830
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:14.250
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.500
I travel to the edge of the world

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:21.960
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.800
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.050
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:31.430
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.100
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:46.700
\hThe One Who Sees All: The Fearsome Fortuneteller, Jin\h

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:46.700
Number 17:

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:47.440
Kaito, this is the new Number’s power.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.910
I am Kaito’s chosen one.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:54.370
I give myself to you.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:06.330
I see the stray lambs.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:12.140
I see who has the next Number.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.810
I’m leaving!

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:24.900
Wait, Yuma!

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.220
Sorry, but I have to shop for my grandma!

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.200
See ya!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.630
Sheesh, he escaped again!

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:35.910
Kotori, we have a good idea.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.910
Numbers Club?

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:42.380
Yeah. We’re going to investigate Numbers.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.840
To summarize, if Yuma isn’t going to talk, then we’ll solve the mystery ourselves.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.470
Sounds like fun!

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:55.250
I’m willing to join the Numbers Club.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.550
Tokunosuke!

00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:00.960
Come to think of it, you once had a Number.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:08.110
Exactly! I’ll share what I remember
when I had a Number.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:09.820
What do you remember?

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:12.840
I don’t remember anything.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:14.780
You...

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:20.170
Umm, I also want to join
the Numbers Club.

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.750
Umm...

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:26.540
I saw Yuma talking by himself.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.460
Was it Astral?

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.300
What was he talking about?

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:33.650
Something about Numbers and defeating Kaito.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:36.020
Kaito? Who’s that?

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:39.570
He may have something to do with the attacks.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:44.150
All right, let’s search for a lead.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.800
Yeah.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.990
It’s the Numbers Club’s first task!

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:51.740
Let’s do it!

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:55.830
If I learn about the Numbers,
Yuma will notice me.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.990
So please!

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:06.670
To summarize, I hate things
that I can’t logically understand.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:10.420
I promise to solve the Number mystery!

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:14.340
If we have the Numbers in our hands…

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.430
Where are they, where are they now?

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:22.810
We’ll show you for sure that we can…

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:26.980
Clear everything up!

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.980
Umm...

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:37.490
You’re investigating Numbers?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:41.950
Shark, please tell me about the Numbers.

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:47.920
They’re cards that you, nor I, can master.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.300
What do you mean?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.760
Don’t get involved with the Numbers.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:00.000
How did it go?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.000
Nothing.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.240
Ditto.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.740
Nothing for me either.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:07.190
To summarize, there were no leads.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:11.650
You weren’t good enough!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:15.650
You can’t find information in the regular world.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.410
Everyone, come with me.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.430
I’ll be the guide.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.290
What is this place?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:27.750
This mansion belongs to a shadowy fortuneteller who’s 100% accurate.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.000
Fortunetelling?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.970
He’ll definitely foretell the Numbers.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:35.720
To summarize, you’re leaving the work to others.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.210
I was waiting for you.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:45.480
Destiny guided you to this mansion.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:53.820
Stray lambs, I’ll use my power
to guide you on the correct path.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:26.420
Umm...

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:29.060
I can see what you want.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:33.020
You’re investigating a certain something.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.330
You know?

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:36.430
Of course!

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:40.450
What you’re looking for is...

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.490
Rectangular and very thin.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:47.160
It’s a card.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:52.650
And it’s not a normal card.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:55.530
It holds incredible power.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:11:01.800
The name of the Duel
Monsters card is... a Number!

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.390
No way!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.900
We didn’t say anything about the Numbers!

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:08.200
Is it a trick?

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.270
How dare you?
Fortunetelling isn’t a trick!

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:16.220
What exactly is a Number?

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:19.380
A Number is an evil thing.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:20.380
Evil?

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:27.820
The Number enters the owner’s heart and eventually takes over his soul.

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:30.620
Yuma’s soul...

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:37.040
Who’s Yuma?

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:46.400
My friend Yuma may be doing something dangerous with the Numbers.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:50.810
That’s why I wanted to know
the Numbers’ secret.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:54.810
I see. Thanks for telling me.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.150
I’m worried about Yuma.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:01.450
Your friend has a Number.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.910
This truly is destiny.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.370
Hey, Kotori.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:10.340
You’ll be sacrificed.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.290
You’re sighing again.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:38.500
How many times was that today?

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:44.060
If you sigh again, I’m going to fine you!

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:44.950
Yuma!

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:46.930
Yuma!

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:47.910
Cat!

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.170
Everyone is...

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:52.040
What happened?

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.290
Kotori and the others were—

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.450
Hey, Cat!

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:01.460
You own a Number.

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.130
This voice...

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:06.420
My name is Jin.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.550
I see through everything.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:11.600
I’m Kaito’s faithful servant.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:13.730
Kaito!

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:17.480
Yuma, I have your friends.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:21.940
You must come to my mansion
and wager your Number in a duel.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:25.320
If you don’t, their lives will be—

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.780
Cat!

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:32.830
Yuma, what happened?

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.910
Cat, take me there!

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.550
Okay!

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:38.830
Wait.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.750
This is a trap.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:44.590
He let her escape so that she’d bring us to him.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:47.010
Who cares if it’s a trap?

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:48.660
Why are you scared?

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.660
I can’t abandon Kotori!

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:53.310
But can you defeat Kaito?

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:58.100
His strategy and skills...

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:01.900
I learned about them in our duel.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.990
There’s no guarantee that we’ll win.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:09.750
You only duel when you have a 100% chance of winning?

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:10.870
Yes.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:15.250
For me, a duel is the same as my life.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:19.190
It’s foolish to battle an opponent when you know you’ll lose.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.210
You...

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:25.170
Unfortunately, you must give up on your friends.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.510
Stop messing around!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.390
Yuma...

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.500
Fine.

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:35.810
I now know how you feel!

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.850
I don’t need your help!

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:48.620
To summarize, where are we?

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.240
Save me!

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.820
Everyone, pull yourself together!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:52.950
Kotori!

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.950
Is it Yuma?

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:57.910
Yuma...

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.770
Kotori!

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.240
What’s that?

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.910
Tetsuo! Everyone!

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:13.210
Welcome, Yuma.

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:15.220
The one who has a Number.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.280
That voice...

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:19.810
Give Kotori back!

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:27.800
If you want to save your friends,
then duel me in front of Kaito.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.840
Kaito...

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:44.590
Astral?

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.210
Kaito!

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:50.300
I’ll take your Number
and give it to Master Kaito!

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.590
What?

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:54.640
I’ll hunt your Number.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.450
Bring it on!

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.250
I promise to win!

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:00.520
I’ll save everyone!

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:03.060
Duel Disk set!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.310
D-Gazer set!

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:09.510
Target locked on!

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:13.000
AR Vision Link complete.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.750
Duel!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.880
I’ll go first.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:25.210
My turn! I draw!

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.250
I summon Orange Shaman.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:41.180
A monster with 0 ATK?

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:45.550
I set one card and end my turn.

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:51.570
Here I go! My turn! I draw!

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:54.490
I summon Gogogo Golem!

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.020
How’s that!

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:03.330
If this attack succeeds, I’ll deal lots of damage with one strike!

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:06.540
I activate Orange Shaman’s effect.

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:13.550
When the opponent summons an Effect Monster, I can Special Summon a Shaman from my hand.

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:16.640
Appear, Red Shaman!

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.010
Another one with 0 ATK.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.270
Be careful, Yuma.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:28.880
What are you talking about?

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:31.860
With 0 ATK, it’s my chance to deal lots of damage!

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:35.360
Go, Gogogo Golem!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:41.910
I flip over my trap card Dance of the Guardian!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:45.560
With this card, I select one card in your hand.

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:49.440
If it’s a monster card, the attack is negated.

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:52.250
I see everything!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:55.880
You won’t succeed
because you’re not a psychic!

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:57.920
Yuma, be careful!

00:17:57.920 --> 00:17:59.600
You have five cards in your hand.

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:03.060
Only one is a monster card.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.390
It’s the second card from the right!

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.940
What?

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:21.530
Due to Dance of the Guardian’s effect, the selected card goes to the graveyard, and I draw a card!

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:24.290
Gagaga Magician went to the graveyard.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:27.670
Can he really see everything?

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:31.880
He saw the only monster card in his hand.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:36.490
Does he really have a power that rivals Kaito’s?

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:46.920
If this keeps up...

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:49.090
Yuma, defend yourself!

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:51.740
Use the trap in your hand
to strengthen your defense!

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:53.980
That’s all I can do for now.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:57.490
I set one card and end my turn!

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:00.110
My turn! I draw!

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:03.450
I activate the spell card Shaman Call.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:10.650
When there are two Spellcaster-Type monsters on my field with 0 ATK...

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:15.050
I can Special Summon one Level 4-or-below Shaman from my deck.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.700
I Special Summon Green Shaman!

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:23.850
What?

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:28.600
This is why he summoned monsters with 0 ATK.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:32.600
Witness my Number’s incredible power!

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:38.590
I overlay Level 4 Orange Shaman, Red Shaman and Green Shaman!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:45.120
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.750
Xyz Summon!

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:53.290
Appear, Number 16!

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:56.290
The ruler of color!

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:06.010
Shock Master!

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.890
That’s his Number!

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.890
I activate Shock Master’s effect!

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:18.080
Once per turn, I can use an Overlay Unit
and choose a card type.

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:22.750
Their card effects are negated
until your second End Phase!

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.630
Negate its effects?

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:26.490
That’s right.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:31.030
The cards I see can’t be used for two turns.

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:34.790
I can see your set card’s type!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.210
This is bad!

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:39.800
Your set card is a trap card!

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:41.510
Impossible!

00:20:50.820 --> 00:20:55.330
Now you can’t stop my attacks.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:02.300
Shock Master attacks Gogogo Golem!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:20.480
Your friends’ lives are connected to your LP.

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:27.640
If you lose, all the rocks will crumble, and they’ll fall into the magma!

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:29.300
What?

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:35.070
Bow before my power and Master Kaito!

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:43.070
I’ll hunt your soul!

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:47.480
Go, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:21:50.020 --> 00:21:51.850
Astral!

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:55.620
This is the end.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.520
I see.

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:01.960
I’m afraid of Kaito.

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:07.070
This is what fear feels like.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:15.440
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:18.370
This week’s quiz:

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:21.810
After using a spell card, do you send it to the graveyard?

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:24.530
Or does it return to the hand?

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:34.790
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:39.920
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:54.370
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:59.540
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:01.940
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.570
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:07.250
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.250 --> 00:23:08.860
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:13.560
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.560 --> 00:23:18.080
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:23.500
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:28.130
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.260
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:37.060
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:43.610
Jin can see everything!

00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:47.400
I’m in huge trouble in this duel!

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:52.450
What? You’ll free Kotori and my friends if I accept defeat and surrender?

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:54.120
Yuma, don’t do it!

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:56.120
Give him the Number... and me.

00:23:56.570 --> 00:23:57.870
Stop joking!

00:23:57.870 --> 00:24:01.510
I want to win for you and your friends!

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:09.970
\h\hChaos Xyz Change! The Light of Hope, Utopia Ray!!\h\h

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:07.090
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Chaos Xyz Change! The Light of Hope, Utopia Ray!!”

00:24:07.480 --> 00:24:09.970
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.930 --> 00:24:14.930
The answer is... send it to the graveyard!

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:22.060
Just like spell cards, used trap cards also go to the graveyard.

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:24.940
Remember that!
